## Summary
Terranigma, the 1995 SNES action-RPG by Quintet, is getting a PC re-release through Clear River Games Development and Limited Run. The author, a self-proclaimed Sega loyalist, sets aside console war grudges to check out the game after colleague Jeremy recommended it.

## Key Points
- Terranigma, originally released for SNES in 1995, is being re-released on PC after 31 years
- Clear River Games Development and Limited Run are partnering on the PC port
- The game was developed by Quintet
- The author acknowledges it as one of their colleague Jeremy's favorite games ever


